        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">This is a readvertisement for JC-462791, with an original&nbsp;Final Filing Date of 2/24/2025. If you previously submitted an application package, it remains under consideration, there is no need to&nbsp;reapply.<br /><br /><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Telework Information:</span></span><span>&nbsp;Hybrid approach that includes office- and remote-centric work solutions.</span></p><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span><br /><span>Do you like working in a collaborative team environment? Are you a dynamic and highly efficient individual? If so, come join the Delta Stewardship Council (Council) contracts team as an Associate Governmental Program Analyst (AGPA). <br /><br />Under the direction of the Staff Services Manager (SSM I), the AGPA is responsible for developing and preparing a diverse workload of contractual agreements ranging from routine to highly technical and complex in accordance with the California Public Contract Code (PCC), Gov Code (GC), Water Code (WC), the State Administrative Manual (SAM), the State Contracting Manual, and departmental operating policies and procedures. The AGPA performs independent analytical work with minimal supervision and will serve as a technical subject matter expert for contracts. The AGPA is also responsible for accurate data entry and data tracking of transactions in Microsoft Excel and other database systems including the Contrakker and Financial Information System for California (Fi$Cal). This position requires the incumbent to work productively in a demanding environment and meet short processing timelines when necessary.<br /> </span></span></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /> </span><div style="box-sizing: border-box; text-decoration-color: initial;"><span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;">We’re located in the new state of the art Natural Resources Building in downtown Sacramento.&nbsp;Our building features ergonomic furniture, panoramic downtown views, a free&nbsp;employee gym, a cafeteria and bodega, call and conference rooms, adjacent childcare, and much more. A hybrid work schedule is available.</span></span></span></div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"></span><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26473207&name=530-001-5393-709and530-001-5157-709DutyStatement.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
